CloudBurrow patch 6 of 6 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bug: #1057, #1017).

Not CloudBurrow's work: this is goccy/googlesqlite pull request #80,
"internal: build path sub-catalogs without the builtin function set", by
@cp-ant, at its head commit fc357c6e11c02f7f9ddc52a940e82bc50039bcb3
(https://github.com/goccy/googlesqlite/pull/80). It is open upstream, not
merged or released. The change is upstream's, unchanged; only the hunk's
line numbers differ, as it is applied to v0.3.1 after patches 1 to 5
rather than to googlesqlite's main at 4dd0bf5.

Why CloudBurrow carries it: every sub-catalog made for a project or dataset
name was built with newSimpleCatalog, which registers the whole GoogleSQL
builtin function set into it, in the engine's WebAssembly memory, which
only grows; every DROP of a table, view or function rebuilds them all
(resetCatalog). The analyzer resolves functions through the root catalog,
so a path sub-catalog is now a bare SimpleCatalog.

